-- Kirchhoff's matrix-tree theorem (1847): the spanning trees of a network are the determinant of its
-- Laplacian with one vertex's row and column struck out; here the first of vs. For r = |vs| − 1 rows the
-- elimination makes Σ_{s=1}^{r−1} s² = (r−1)r(2r−1)/6 entry updates, each two products, one difference and
-- one exact quotient, and building the matrix reads the m lines once for each of its r² entries.
kirchhoff : List Nat → List FaradayLine → Nat
kirchhoff vs ls = bareiss (vertex-count vs) (suc zero) (lap-rows ls (drop-first vs) (drop-first vs))
